<p><strong>Network Access Control List (network ACL)</strong></p>

<p>A Network Access Control List (network ACL) is an optional layer of secu=
rity for your virtual private cloud (VPC) that acts as a firewall for contr=
olling traffic in and out of one or more subnets (i.e. it works at the subn=
et level). A network ACL has separate inbound and outbound rules, and each =
rule can either allow or deny traffic.</p>

