ill not help with fault tolerance.</p>

<p><strong>Distributing load to Amazon EC2 instances</strong> - Even though=
 this helps with fault tolerance and is often used with Amazon EC2 Auto Sca=
ling, it is a feature of Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) and not an Amazon EC2=
 Auto Scaling. Elastic Load Balancing automatically distributes incoming ap=
plication traffic across multiple targets, such as Amazon EC2 instances, co=
ntainers, IP addresses, and Lambda functions. It can handle the varying loa=
d of your application traffic in a single Availability Zone (AZ) or across =
multiple Availability Zones (AZs).</p>

<p><strong>Having the right amount of computing capacity</strong> - Amazon =
EC2 Auto Scaling ensures that your application always has the right amount =
of computing capacity, so your application can handle the workload.</p>

